<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hell-Ville</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Andoany</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hell-Ville, officially Andoany, is the main town of the island of Nosy Be off north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. It was named after Admiral Anne Chrétien Louis de Hell, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> (Réunion), under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> took possession of Nosy Be in 1841. It is a port and the centre of the island's tourism and of its production of vanilla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and the perfume plant ylang-ylang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hell-ville.jpg" alt="Hell-Ville" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MauritsV (Maurits Vermeulen) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hellville_Nosy_Be_Madagascar_at_dusk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
